BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-videotage-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T232015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Videotage 2027 (Ho
 ng Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) runs this r
 esidency with Videotage\, a Hong Kong-based non-profit media arts institut
 ion specialising in the promotion\, presentation\, creation and preservati
 on of moving image and media art in all forms and languages. The Fund is r
 ecruiting one Netherlands-based designer\, maker or observer working in di
 gital culture to spend two or three months at Videotage's studio space in 
 Hong Kong in 2027\, conducting research\, broadening their network\, devel
 oping new work inspired by Hong Kong\, and presenting their findings or co
 mpleted works. The residency encourages crossovers and experimentation\, g
 iving the participant space to explore new methodologies\, widen their cre
 ative practice and produce work that pushes the boundaries of digital cult
 ure\, with a focus on social and urban dynamics. The 2027 edition takes th
 e technological 'black box' phenomenon as its starting point and invites t
 he resident to respond to that theme within the context of Videotage. ELIG
 IBILITY: you are an individual designer\, maker or observer within the fie
 ld of digital culture\; you are established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, B
 onaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the N
 etherlands)\; you are registered in the business register of the Dutch Cha
 mber of Commerce (KvK) or another business register within the Kingdom of 
 the Netherlands\; and you have had a professional practice in the creative
  industry for at least four years. NOT open to duos\, collectives or coope
 rative ventures\, nor to designers and makers who receive a grant during t
 he work period under the Talent Development Grant Scheme\, the Open Call S
 elf-taught Designer or the Open Call Emerging Design Practices ABCSSS. Not
 e that accepting this open call means you cannot apply to those schemes an
 d open calls in 2027. FUNDING: EUR 5\,000 for two months or EUR 6\,500 for
  three months\, covering travel\, insurance\, living expenses\, compensati
 on for time invested and material and transport costs\; accommodation\, st
 udio use and Videotage's facilitation are covered separately by the Fund. 
 Submit your proposal to the Creative Industries Fund NL by 21 October 2026
 \, 16:00 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Cre
 ative Industries Fund NL) in collaboration with Videotage\, Hong Kong\nLoc
 ation: Residency takes place at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must be
  established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint 
 Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a
  business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 5\,0
 00 for a two-month residency or EUR 6\,500 for a three-month residency\, p
 aid by the Creative Industries Fund NL to cover travel\, insurance\, livin
 g expenses\, compensation for time invested\, and material and transport c
 osts. Accommodation\, use of the studio space and facilitation by Videotag
 e are covered directly by the Fund on top of this. No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Two or three months in 2027 (spring 2027)\; state your preferred p
 eriod in the application.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/gra
 nts/open-call-videotage?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must b
 e established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint
  Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in 
 a business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:yao-residency-02-taiwan-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T232015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: YAO Residency #02 (Taiwan): Research Residency 2027 and E
 xhibition 2028
DESCRIPTION:YAO Residency #02 centres on the translation between culture an
 d material: through living\, research and exchange in Taiwan\, artists eng
 age with different cultural contexts\, local ways of living\, materials an
 d craft practices\, with emphasis on process rather than finished works. O
 NE artist/practitioner is selected for a two-phase program. PHASE ONE (res
 earch residency\, 21 August to 21 November 2027): field research\, materia
 l exploration and local engagement\, closing with an Open Studio (27 Octob
 er to 16 November 2027) presenting research in progress. PHASE TWO (2028):
  the artist returns to Taiwan for a formal exhibition or other public pres
 entation at YAO\, expected to run at least six weeks. WHAT YOU GET: per ph
 ase\, travel support (international applicants up to NTD 20\,000 round-tri
 p against receipts)\, a living stipend of NTD 10\,000 and accommodation\; 
 Phase One adds a production budget of up to NTD 20\,000\, an Open Studio v
 enue and help connecting with craftspeople\, communities and cultural prac
 titioners\; Phase Two adds the exhibition venue\, installation assistance 
 and documentation\; both phases include text editing\, translation and pro
 motional support. ELIGIBILITY: artists\, makers\, researchers and interdis
 ciplinary practitioners aged 18 or over with an ongoing creative practice\
 , any nationality\; suited to self-directed researchers who transform rese
 arch into artistic practice. APPLICATION: via Google Form as a single PDF 
 with CV\, artist statement\, portfolio and a residency proposal covering m
 ethodology\, research themes\, areas of Taiwan engagement (materials\, cra
 fts\, environments\, cultural contexts)\, planned activities and possible 
 creative directions\; in Mandarin or English. FEE: NTD 300 (Taiwan-based\,
  bank transfer) or USD 10 (international\, PayPal)\, non-refundable\; uplo
 ad proof of payment. TIMELINE: interview invitations 10 January 2027\, onl
 ine interviews 16 January\, selection announced 29 January 2027. DEADLINE:
  31 December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: YAO Residency Program (Yao Zuo Zhu Cun
  Ji Hua)\nLocation: Taiwan. Open worldwide to applicants aged 18 and above
 \, regardless of nationality\; international artists arrange their own ent
 ry and visa (YAO can provide an invitation letter).\nAward: Research Resid
 ency 2027: travel support (international applicants reimbursed up to NTD 2
 0\,000 for one round-trip to Taiwan against receipts)\, production budget 
 up to NTD 20\,000\, living stipend of NTD 10\,000\, accommodation\, Open S
 tudio venue\, local connections\, and documentation\, text editing\, trans
 lation and promotional support. Exhibition Phase 2028: travel support up t
 o NTD 20\,000 again\, a further NTD 10\,000 living stipend\, accommodation
 \, exhibition venue at YAO\, installation and de-installation assistance\,
  and exhibition documentation. Application fee: NTD 300 for Taiwan-based a
 pplicants (bank transfer) or USD 10 for international applicants (PayPal)\
 , non-refundable.\nDuration: Two phases: research residency 21 August to 2
 1 November 2027 with Open Studio 27 October to 16 November 2027\, then a f
 ormal exhibition at YAO in 2028 (expected to run at least six weeks\, date
 s agreed with the artist). The selected artist commits to both phases.\n\n
 More: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQ5-RBrfPckf4O9A5LeDrAzbFl
 XHzBkYrpPyTiy3HeKc8BkQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQ5-RBrfPckf4O9A5LeDrAzbFlXHz
 BkYrpPyTiy3HeKc8BkQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Taiwan. Open worldwide to applicants aged 18 and above\, regardles
 s of nationality\; international artists arrange their own entry and visa 
 (YAO can provide an invitation letter).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cifnl-videotage-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T232015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Industries Fund NL: Residency Videotage 2027 (Ho
 ng Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL offers one residency at Videota
 ge\, the Hong Kong media art institute (est. 1986) known for critical work
  on XR\, AI\, blockchain and video games. The 2027 edition takes the techn
 ological 'black box' phenomenon as its starting point: deep neural network
 s now shape social media\, healthcare\, finance\, governance and justice w
 hile their inner workings remain hard to grasp\, and the resident is invit
 ed to explore this through media art in Hong Kong's urban context. WHO: an
  individual designer\, maker or observer within digital culture\, establis
 hed in the Netherlands or the Caribbean parts of the Kingdom\, registered 
 with the KvK (or another Kingdom business register)\, with at least four y
 ears of professional practice. NOT for duos\, collectives\, or recipients 
 of CIFNL Talent Development\, Self-taught Designer or Emerging Design Prac
 tices ABCSSS grants during the work period (winning this excludes applying
  to those schemes in 2027). SUPPORT: EUR 5\,000 (two months) or EUR 6\,500
  (three months) for travel\, insurance\, living costs\, time and materials
 \; housing\, workspace\, curatorial guidance and production costs are paid
  directly to Videotage\; accommodation arranged by Videotage\; access to e
 quipment and the Videotage Media Art Collection archive. SELECTION: tender
 -style ranking by an external advisory committee on artistic quality\, pro
 ject quality and motivation\; the top five proposals go to Videotage\, whi
 ch co-decides\; decision within eight weeks of closing. APPLY via the Fund
 's application platform (aanvragen.stimuleringsfonds.nl)\, round 'Open Cal
 l Residencies 2027'\, preferably in English: work plan (max 4 A4 / 4 MB PD
 F)\, brief CV (max 2 A4)\, portfolio (max 8 A4 / 8 MB)\, certified KvK ext
 ract under one year old\, and a representative JPG image. NOTE: account ac
 tivation on the platform takes one working day\, so register early. DEADLI
 NE: 21 October 2026\, 16:00 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: Creative Industries Fun
 d NL (Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie)\, with Videotage\nLocation: H
 ong Kong (Videotage premises). Only for applicants established in the Neth
 erlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarte
 n and registered with a Kingdom of the Netherlands business register (KvK)
 .\nAward: One residency grant: EUR 5\,000 for a two-month work period or E
 UR 6\,500 for three months\, covering travel\, insurance\, living expenses
 \, compensation for time invested\, and material and transport costs. Hous
 ing\, work space\, Videotage guidance and production costs are paid by the
  Fund directly to Videotage on top of the grant\; accommodation is arrange
 d by Videotage. No application fee.\nDuration: 23 March to 18 May 2027 (tw
 o months) or 23 March to 15 June 2027 (three months)\; state your preferre
 d period. Research period plus a concluding public presentation event for 
 Videotage's Hong Kong network.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/e
 n/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hong Kong (Videotage premises). Only for applicants established in
  the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Si
 nt Maarten and registered with a Kingdom of the Netherlands business regis
 ter (KvK).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tarbell-fellowship-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T232015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tarbell Fellowship 2027-28 (AI journalism)
DESCRIPTION:A year-long fellowship for journalists covering artificial inte
 lligence. Fellows complete a three-month full-time remote programme on AI 
 and journalism fundamentals\, attend a weeklong summit\, then work for nin
 e months as reporters embedded in a partner newsroom (current partners are
  in Hong Kong\, London\, Los Angeles\, New York\, San Francisco\, Seattle\
 , Washington DC and Cambridge). ELIGIBILITY: journalism or AI expertise\, 
 aged 18+ by 7 June 2027\, no degree required\; primarily for applicants wi
 th the right to work in the US\, UK or Hong Kong\, as visa sponsorship is 
 uncommon and needs partner-outlet approval.\n\nOrganisation: Tarbell Cente
 r for AI Journalism\nLocation: Remote training\, then newsroom placement i
 n the US\, UK or Hong Kong. In person.\nAward: USD 75\,000 to 120\,000 dep
 ending on experience and placement cost of living\; senior fellows (7+ yea
 rs experience) USD 115\,000 to 135\,000. Summit travel and accommodation c
 overed. No application fee.\nDuration: 12 months: remote training 7 June t
 o 6 August 2027\, in-person summit August 2027\, newsroom placement Septem
 ber 2027 to May 2028 (extendable by one year).\n\nMore: https://www.tarbel
 lcenter.org/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://www.tarbellcenter.org/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote training\, then newsroom placement in the US\, UK or Hong K
 ong. In person.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mplus-sigg-fellowship-chinese-art-research-2026-27@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20261024T232015Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:Deadline: M+ Sigg Fellowship for Chinese Art Research 2026/27 (HKD 
 200\,000\, Hong Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Sigg Fellowship for Chinese Art Research supports new resea
 rch on Chinese art in dialogue with the M+ Collections\; the 2026/27 editi
 on focuses on tradition and contemporary Chinese art. WHO: individuals or 
 research groups of any nationality and any age\, with a postgraduate degre
 e in a relevant discipline\, or an undergraduate degree plus at least thre
 e years of relevant professional or academic research experience\; profici
 ency in spoken and written Chinese or English is required\, and the fellow
 ship is subject to obtaining a Hong Kong visa. WHAT YOU GET: HKD 200\,000 
 to cover all expenses\, including travel\, living\, insurance and research
  costs\, for a three-to-six-month attachment to M+. Fellows give a public 
 lecture in Hong Kong and write an essay of at least 5\,000 English words o
 r 7\,500 Chinese characters for M+ Magazine. APPLICATION: submit a researc
 h proposal (max 1\,000 words) and full CV via the Google form on the call 
 page\, in English or Chinese\, and have two academic or professional refer
 ees email recommendation letters directly. Results are announced in early 
 2027. DEADLINE: 30 November 2026\, 23:59 (UTC+8).\n\nOrganisation: M+\, We
 st Kowloon Cultural District\nLocation: Hong Kong. Open to individuals or 
 research groups of any nationality\; the fellowship depends on obtaining a
  Hong Kong visa.\nAward: HKD 200\,000 covering all expenses (travel\, livi
 ng\, insurance and research costs). No application fee mentioned.\nDuratio
 n: 3 to 6 months attached to M+ in Hong Kong.\n\nMore: https://www.mplus.o
 rg.hk/en/awards-and-fellowships/sigg-fellowship-for-chinese-art-research/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mplus.org.hk/en/awards-and-fellowships/sigg-fellowship-for-
 chinese-art-research/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
LOCATION:Hong Kong. Open to individuals or research groups of any nationali
 ty\; the fellowship depends on obtaining a Hong Kong visa.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
